.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our functions.\n\n- The domain of $p$ is ${2,4},$ the set containing the two numbers $2$ and $4$ only.\n\n- The domain of $q$ is $[2,4],$ the interval from $2$ to $4$ (including $2$ and $4$).\n\n- The domain of $r$ is $R,$ the set of real numbers.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360715 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172034 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1240e42a-92a5-51cc-a80e-3fe1ef0b16f7" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Codomains and Ranges"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c8d9fe4-748c-5102-bb51-a28ffdcbaf8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358273} {:answer/id #uuid "81f08277-6d3c-5798-8f59-adda0f03c5b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358887} {:answer/id #uuid "92c84071-d08c-5db6-b132-dc8441bfe820" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359036} {:answer/id #uuid "98f1a428-f368-5112-a8ed-b303f7b5a821" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359094} {:answer/id #uuid "dbb9db4a-78cc-5b0a-8478-df90071bb946" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359677}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98f1a428-f368-5112-a8ed-b303f7b5a821" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359094} :answer-field/id #uuid "662a29b1-6500-5da6-aab3-9ef7fb0ee549" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360158}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "777628a7-f0f2-562d-ab61-872a852162b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-96825" :question/problem "Which of the following is the correct interpretation of $f:[-1,1]\\to R?$\n\n- The domain of $f$ is $[-1,1]$\n- The codomain of $f$ is $[-1,1]$\n- The range of $f$ is $R$" :question/worked-solution "The notation \n\n$$\nf:[-1,1]\\to R\n$$\n\nmeans that the function $f$ maps the set $[-1,1]$ to the set $R.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $[-1,1],$ and\n\n- the codomain of $f$ is $R.$ Note that this is *not* necessarily the range.\n\nAs a result, statements II and III are false, while statement I is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360716 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172034 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1240e42a-92a5-51cc-a80e-3fe1ef0b16f7" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Codomains and Ranges"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "397831d8-e13d-594b-bace-3e4605e182d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358259} {:answer/id #uuid "53167b65-f20e-5101-9bd3-713b6ff0cff0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358468} {:answer/id #uuid "5a7774c7-4f3f-5929-91d3-a3a4394f95f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358536} {:answer/id #uuid "6005c77b-139d-59b4-b669-65a3af94d660" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358591} {:answer/id #uuid "ec08de58-09a9-5ec2-b6d2-cd16df044e80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359854}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "397831d8-e13d-594b-bace-3e4605e182d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358259} :answer-field/id #uuid "f976bda8-294e-5535-9c86-f528545d4614" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360436}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "af009dba-f7f5-5f73-94d4-82504fdd6317" :question/math-academy-id "q-96826" :question/problem "Which of the following is the correct interpretation of $g:R\\to R?$\n\n- The domain of $g$ is $R$\n- The codomain of $g$ is $R$\n- The range of $g$ is $R$" :question/worked-solution "The notation \n\n$$\ng:R\\to R\n$$\n\nmeans that the function $g$ maps the set $R$ to the set $R.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $g$ is $R,$ and\n\n- the codomain of $g$ is $R.$ Note that this is *not* necessarily the range.\n\nAs a result, statements I and II are true, while statement III is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360717 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172034 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1240e42a-92a5-51cc-a80e-3fe1ef0b16f7" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Codomains and Ranges"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07f246b6-2551-5431-99fd-a922df23836e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357823} {:answer/id #uuid "1cbd9456-f8d1-5ba2-b964-9373c0c86d28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357999} {:answer/id #uuid "3caea4e3-6736-5052-9ab6-db7e72fd721e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358274} 